      "cat": "tool",
      "author": "crosire · guide by Echelon",
      "date": "2019-04-28",
      "note": "Not a skin. It grades the whole rendered frame — bloom, sharpening, colour, ambient occlusion — and you tune it live in-game. PSOBB draws in Direct3D 8, so d3d8to9 has to sit in the folder first for ReShade to attach at all. Echelon's Modern PSO preset is the usual starting point.",
      "noteKey": "mod.n.reshade",
      "warn": "The shaders sit on top of everything, so the HUD and Lua addons get graded too and addon text can become hard to read. Turn off any compatibility mode on PSOBB.exe first — it stops ReShade attaching, and a few people have hit crashes from the renderer setting in the launcher.",
      "warnKey": "mod.w.reshade",
      "install": [
        "Put d3d8to9's d3d8.dll in your game folder.",
        "Run the ReShade installer, point it at PSOBB.exe and pick Direct3D 9.",
        "Choose the effect packs you want when it asks.",
        "Launch the game and press Home to open the ReShade menu. Load Echelon's preset if you would rather not tune it yourself."
